        "original_id": "a0c8b2b0-6cd9-5e43-860e-efdfcaaf385e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: French Montana, Machine Gun Kelly, MGK, Richard Colson Baker, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg, Lee on the Beats, DJ Khaled, Bkorn\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That, Hold You Down\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Topics: guest appearances, music production, mixtapes\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Colson Baker was born on April 22, 1990, and he is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio who is better known as MGK or Machine Gun Kelly.\n- Machine Gun Kelly began his music career as a teenager and released a mixtape in 2006.\n- French Montana released his debut studio album Excuse My French in 2013.\n- The album Excuse My French features guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg.\n- Pop That was released as the first single from Excuse My French and features Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.\n- Lee on the Beats is best known for producing French Montana’s Pop That and for co-producing DJ Khaled’s Hold You Down with Bkorn.",
